Sources/BasaltCore/ModelOrchestratorActor.swift:Task.detached: the stream relay outlives generateStream and must not run on the orchestrator actor or inherit its priority, or every chunk would queue behind other requests; it holds only Sendable values, reaches actor state only through await self.finish, and is cancelled by the gate and by stream termination
Sources/BasaltInference/MLXInferenceEngine.swift:Task.detached: the token stream task outlives the engine call and must not inherit the engine actor's isolation or priority; it carries only the Sendable parts of the GenerationLaunch (stream, decode task, counters), the caches stay on the actor under the lease id, and keep and recycle hand state back on the actor
Sources/BasaltServer/MCP/MCPServer.swift:Thread: readLine blocks, so stdin is read on its own thread instead of a cooperative-pool thread; it touches only the AsyncStream continuation and an Atomic stop flag
Sources/BasaltUI/ClipboardManager.swift:Thread: writing a large input to the child's stdin pipe blocks until the child reads it, while this thread drains stdout; the writer thread owns only the pipe handle and the bytes it writes
